    "top_description": `<div class="landing-page-header-container col-xs-12 col-sm-12 col-md-12 col-lg-9 col-xl-9"><p dir="ltr">Shop our extensive range of vacuum cleaner bags at Statewide Appliance Spares. <span class="collection-read-more"> Read more</span></p></div>`,
    "below_description": `<div class="landing-page-header-container col-xs-12 col-sm-12 col-md-12 col-lg-9 col-xl-9"><p><meta charset="utf-8"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta charset="utf-8">Discover Australia’s most extensive range of vacuum parts and accessories, tailored for every floor care need. From versatile backpack and barrel vacuums to cutting-edge robotic models, we’ve got you covered. For over 40 years, Statewide Appliance Spares has been at the forefront of appliance spare parts, offering competitively priced solutions for leading brands like Electrolux, LG, Miele, Vax, and Volta.&nbsp;</p><h2 class="contenthead" dir="ltr"><span>What type of bag do I need for my vacuum cleaner?</span></h2><p dir="ltr"><span>The type of bag you need for your vacuum cleaner depends on the specific model and brand of your vacuum cleaner. Different vacuum cleaners utilise different types of bags and it's important to use the appropriate bag recommended by the manufacturer to ensure proper performance and compatibility.</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span>Here are a few common types of vacuum cleaner bags:</span></p><ol><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><strong>Paper Bags:</strong><span>&nbsp;These bags are made of paper material and are commonly used in many traditional upright and canister vacuum cleaners. They are generally disposable and should be replaced when full or when suction power decreases.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><strong>Cloth Bags:</strong><span>&nbsp;Some vacuum cleaners use cloth or fabric bags that can be washed and reused. These bags are typically more durable and environmentally friendly. They require regular cleaning to maintain their performance.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><strong>HEPA Bags:</strong><span>&nbsp;High-Efficiency Particulate Air (HEPA) bags are designed to trap and contain fine particles, allergens, and pollutants, providing improved air filtration. They are often used in vacuum cleaners for people with allergies or asthma. HEPA bags are available in both paper and cloth varieties.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><strong>Bagless Systems:</strong><span>&nbsp;Some vacuum cleaners feature a bagless design, eliminating the need for disposable bags. These models use filters or collection containers that can be emptied and cleaned after use. However, it's important to clean and maintain the filters regularly for optimal performance.</span></p></li></ol><h2 class="contenthead" dir="ltr"><span>How do I change the bag in my vacuum cleaner?</span></h2><p dir="ltr"><span>The process of changing the bag in a vacuum cleaner can vary slightly depending on the specific model and brand. However, here are general steps to guide you through the process:</span></p><ol><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><span>Ensure that you have a replacement bag that is compatible with your vacuum cleaner model. Refer to the manufacturer's instructions or user manual for the correct bag type and size.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><span>Turn off and unplug your vacuum cleaner to ensure safety during the bag changing process.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><span>Locate the Bag Compartment: Depending on the design of your vacuum cleaner, the bag compartment may be located on the front, rear, or side of the unit. Look for a latch, door, or release mechanism that provides access to the bag compartment.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><span>Open the Bag Compartment. Use the latch, release button, or other mechanisms to open the bag compartment. This may involve lifting a cover, sliding a door, or removing a panel.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><span>Once the bag compartment is open, carefully remove the full bag from the vacuum cleaner. Some models may have a bag retaining clip or strap to hold the bag in place, so release or unhook it if necessary.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><span>If you're using disposable bags, seal the full bag and dispose of it properly according to your local waste disposal guidelines. If you have a reusable bag, empty its contents into a garbage bag or rubbish bin.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><span>Take the new bag and prepare it according to the manufacturer's instructions. Some bags may require unfolding or attaching specific clips or adapters.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><span>Insert the new bag into the bag compartment, ensuring it is properly aligned and fitted. Follow any specific instructions provided by the manufacturer.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><span>Close and secure the bag compartment door, latch, or cover until it clicks or locks into place. Ensure that it is properly sealed to prevent dust and debris from escaping.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><span>Take a moment to clean any debris or dust that may have accumulated around the bag compartment or in other accessible parts of the vacuum cleaner. This will help maintain the cleanliness and performance of the unit.</span></p></li></ol><h2 class="contenthead" dir="ltr"><span>Can I use a generic bag instead of the brand specific one?</span></h2><p dir="ltr"><span>It is generally recommended to use the vacuum bags suggested by the manufacturer.</span></p><ul><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><strong>Brand-specific vacuum cleaner bags</strong><span>&nbsp;are designed to fit the specific dimensions and attachments of your vacuum cleaner model. Generic bags may not have the same fit, which can lead to issues such as improper sealing, reduced suction power, or even damage to the vacuum cleaner.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><span>Vacuum cleaner bags play a crucial role in filtration and dust containment. Brand-specific bags are often designed to provide optimal filtration and dust retention, ensuring that the vacuum cleaner operates efficiently and effectively. Generic bags may not have the same level of filtration or dust containment capabilities, which can impact the cleaning performance and air quality.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><span>Specific bags are typically manufactured to meet the quality standards and specifications set by the vacuum cleaner manufacturer. They undergo testing to ensure durability and reliability. Generic bags may vary in quality, and some may not be as durable or long-lasting, potentially leading to premature failure or the need for more frequent replacements.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation"><span>Using non-brand-specific bags may void the warranty provided by the manufacturer. In case of any issues or malfunctions, the manufacturer may not provide support or cover any damages resulting from the use of generic bags.</span></p></li></ul><p dir="ltr"><span>Experience the Statewide advantage – the biggest range in Australia, fast delivery, lowest price guarantee and expert guidance from our local team. At Statewide Appliance Spares, we make buying spares easier!</span></p><p dir="ltr">&nbsp;</p></div>`,
